\section{Reviews, feedback and reflections}

A row of the default output is a reviewer's assessment of one reviewee on
one criterion: the level chosen, if the criterion is a rubric, and the
comments written.
FBF keeps the level and the comments apart, as a rating and as reviews, but
a reader wants them together, so a [[Review]] holds both.
It names the people rather than holding their ids, since the names are what
the output shows.
A [[Comment]] keeps what it is about ([[on]]: the activity as a whole or a
submitted file) and when it was written.

<<imports>>=
import dataclasses
<<classes>>=
@dataclasses.dataclass
class Comment:
    """A reviewer's comment on one criterion."""

    on: str
    created: str
    body: str


@dataclasses.dataclass
class Review:
    """A reviewer's level and comments on one criterion for a reviewee."""

    activity: str
    reviewee: str
    reviewer: str
    criterion: str
    level: str = ""
    score: int = None
    comments: list = dataclasses.field(default_factory=list)
