\section{Feedback on the reviews}

A reviewee may rate each review received, if the activity allows it.
When it does not, the view task's [[reviewer-feedback-enabled]] is false
and we send no requests at all; the command says so.
When it does, each allocation that has a review may have feedback, and
since the allocation has no count for it we have to ask each one.

<<functions>>=
def feedback_enabled(tasks):
    """Tell whether the reviewees may rate the reviews they got."""
    task = tasks.get(VIEW_TASK)
    return bool(task and attribute(task, "reviewer-feedback-enabled"))


def reviewed(allocation):
    """Tell whether the reviewer of `allocation` wrote or rated anything."""
    return bool(attribute(allocation, "reviews-count")
                or attribute(allocation, "ratings-count"))


def fetch_feedback(fbf, tasks, activity):
    """Return the `Feedback` on the reviews of a peer-review activity."""
    if not feedback_enabled(tasks):
        return []
    allocations = fbf.get(related_link(tasks[REVIEW_TASK],
                                       "allocations")).resources
    users = allocation_users(fbf, allocations)
    lists = allocation_lists(fbf, allocations,
                             {"reviewer-feedback": reviewed})
    return make_feedback(activity, allocations, lists["reviewer-feedback"],
                         users)
@

A feedback belongs to an allocation, which names the reviewer and the
reviewee.

<<functions>>=
def make_feedback(activity, allocations, feedbacks, users):
    """Return the `Feedback`s, sorted by reviewee and reviewer."""
    by_id = {allocation["id"]: allocation for allocation in allocations}
    result = []
    for feedback in feedbacks:
        allocation = by_id[related_id(feedback, "allocation")]
        result.append(Feedback(
            activity,
            name_of(users, person(allocation, "allocable")),
            name_of(users, person(allocation, "actor")),
            attribute(feedback, "rating"),
            plain_text(attribute(feedback, "body"))))
    return sorted(result, key=lambda f: (f.reviewee, f.reviewer))
