\section{Output}

The output follows [[canvaslms]], as in \cref{Discussions}: one row per
item, fields separated by the delimiter, tab by default.
By default a row is a [[Review]]: the activity, the reviewee, the reviewer,
the criterion, the level, the score, and the comments joined by
[[ | ]].
With [[--long]] every comment gets a row of its own, with what it is about
and when it was written, which is what reading the comments needs.
A review that has a level but no comment still gets a row then, with the
comment's fields empty, so that [[--long]] shows everything the default
does.
Line breaks in a text would break the rows, so we fold them into spaces.
The score is the option's weight as FBF stores it; how FBF turns weights
into a grade we do not know, so we do not add them up.

<<constants>>=
COMMENT_SEPARATOR = " | "
<<functions>>=
def review_rows(reviews, long=False):
    """Yield output rows (lists of strings) for `reviews`."""
    for review in reviews:
        head = [review.activity, review.reviewee, review.reviewer,
                review.criterion, review.level,
                "" if review.score is None else str(review.score)]
        if not long:
            yield head + [COMMENT_SEPARATOR.join(fold(c.body)
                                                 for c in review.comments)]
            continue
        for comment in review.comments or [Comment("", "", "")]:
            yield head + [comment.on, comment.created, fold(comment.body)]


def fold(text):
    """Return `text` on one line, runs of white space made one space."""
    return " ".join(text.split())
@

